.TH KWAAINET 1 "2026-09-09" "KwaaiNet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kwaainet \- KwaaiNet node CLI for decentralized inference and training
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kwaainet
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kwaainet
runs and controls a node on KwaaiNet, a libp2p peer-to-peer network for
sovereign AI: decentralized model inference, distributed transformer block
sharding, and private vector storage.
.PP
A node joins the network through bootstrap peers, announces the model blocks it
can serve, and discovers other nodes over a distributed hash table. Nodes behind
NAT connect via hole punching or relay circuits, so no port forwarding is
required in the common case.
.PP
The p2p stack runs inside the node process; there is no separate daemon to
install. Configuration and state, including the node identity key, live under
.IR ~/.kwaainet .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start the KwaaiNet node.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the KwaaiNet daemon.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the KwaaiNet daemon.
.TP
.B run\-node
Run the node in the foreground. This is the entry point the auto\-start
service uses; prefer
.B start
interactively.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status.
.TP
.B logs
Show daemon logs.
.TP
.B config
View or modify configuration.
.TP
.B node\-health
Live health check: Ollama and relay circuit status.
.TP
.B service
Manage the auto\-start service. This package installs no service;
.B service install
writes a systemd user unit under
.IR ~/.config/systemd/user .
.TP
.B p2p
Inspect live p2p state, such as identity and connected peers.
.TP
.B shard
Distributed transformer block sharding: serve a range of blocks, coordinate
inference across peers, or inspect block coverage on the network.
.TP
.B serve
Serve an OpenAI\-compatible API backed by the local model.
.TP
.B storage
Manage the local storage fabric.
.TP
.B vpk
Manage VPK (Virtual Private Knowledge) vector database integration.
.TP
.B update
Check for a newer release. On a packaged install it prints the command that
upgrades the package instead of installing anything; see
.B NOTES
below.
.TP
.B uninstall
Stop the node and remove its data. On a packaged install the binary itself is
left to the package manager.
.PP
This is not the full command set. Run
.B kwaainet \-\-help
for the complete list, and
.BI "kwaainet " COMMAND " \-\-help"
for the options of any one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KWAAINET_NO_AUTO_UPDATE
When set to
.BR 1 ,
a running node never downloads or installs an update in the background. A
packaged install already behaves this way; the variable is a developer
escape hatch for unpackaged builds.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.BR kwaainet=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/config.yaml
Node configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/identity.key
Node identity key. Never removed by package upgrade or removal.
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/logs/kwaainet.log
Node log.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/kwaainet/packaged
Marker, containing
.BR deb ,
that tells
.B kwaainet
it was installed from a package. While it is present, and the binary is
.IR /usr/bin/kwaainet ,
self\-update and self\-uninstall are disabled.
.SH NOTES
This package installs KwaaiNet from a distribution package. Self\-update is
disabled, because it would replace files the package manager owns.
.B kwaainet update
still reports a newer release and prints the
.BR dpkg (1)
command that installs it; remove with
.BR apt (8).
See
.I /usr/share/doc/kwaainet/README.Debian
for details.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
